#: ../../../reference/extensions/python_api/CommandAPI.rst:2
msgid "Command API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../common/experimental_warning.inc:3
msgid ""
"This feature is experimental and subject to breaking changes. See :ref:`the "
"Conan stability<stability>` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../common/subapi_instantiation_warning.inc:3
msgid ""
"Subapis **must not** be initialized by themselves. They are intended to be "
"accessed only through the main :ref:`ConanAPI "
"<reference_python_api_conan_api>` attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../conan_sources/conan/api/subapi/command.py:docstring of
#: conan.api.subapi.command.CommandAPI:1
msgid ""
"This CommandAPI is useful to be able to launch full commands from the "
"ConanAPI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../conan_sources/conan/api/subapi/command.py:docstring of
#: conan.api.subapi.command.CommandAPI:3
msgid ""
"Sometimes some commands are built using several calls to the ConanAPI. If we "
"want to reuse the same functionality, then we would have to copy all that "
"code into our own commands. Instead of doing that, it is possible to call "
"Conan commands using this API, via the ``run()`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../conan_sources/conan/api/subapi/command.py:docstring of
#: conan.api.subapi.command.CommandAPI.run:1
msgid "Runs another Conan command via API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../conan_sources/conan/api/subapi/command.py:docstring of
#: conan.api.subapi.command.CommandAPI.run:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../conan_sources/conan/api/subapi/command.py:docstring of
#: conan.api.subapi.command.CommandAPI.run:3
msgid "Conan command to run. It can be either a string, or a list of strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../conan_sources/conan/api/subapi/command.py:docstring of
#: conan.api.subapi.command.CommandAPI.run:4
msgid ""
"If True, it will raise an exception on errors. By default, some command will "
"return errors as ``conan_error`` entries in the result, and it will be the "
"caller's responsibility to check for them and raise/report them if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../conan_sources/conan/api/subapi/command.py:docstring of
#: conan.api.subapi.command.CommandAPI.run:0
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../conan_sources/conan/api/subapi/command.py:docstring of
#: conan.api.subapi.command.CommandAPI.run:7
msgid ""
"It will return what that command returns. Note that different commands can "
"return different things, so the caller needs to process it accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/extensions/python_api/CommandAPI.rst:16
msgid ""
"When consuming this sub-API from a standalone script where the ``ConanAPI`` "
"class is instantiated manually (which is not the recommended way to use the "
"Python API, and :ref:`custom commands<reference_commands_custom_commands>` "
"should be preferred), an extra step is required, because the ``ConanAPI`` "
"class does not automatically set the CLI interface needed for this sub-API "
"to work properly. In that case, the following code snippet should be used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/extensions/python_api/CommandAPI.rst:21
msgid ""
"from conan.api.conan_api import ConanAPI\n"
"from conan.cli.cli import Cli\n"
"\n"
"api = ConanAPI()\n"
"cli = Cli(api)\n"
"cli.add_commands()\n"
"result = api.command.run([\"remote\", \"list\"])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/extensions/python_api/CommandAPI.rst:33
msgid ""
"The ``Cli`` class should be treated as a private opaque object, and its "
"usage limited to the above snippet."
msgstr ""
